const DREAM_RULE_EN559=[
'You learn the subclass table’s spells when you reach the indicated Sorcerer level. They count as Sorcerer spells for you and do not count against your chosen-spell limit. In the Codex, they remain always prepared. Whenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one spell granted by this feature with another of the same level from the Enchantment or Illusion school on the Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard spell list.',
'When you finish a Long Rest, choose a number of friendly creatures you can see equal to your Charisma modifier and roll on the dream table to determine a dream about their fate. Each chosen creature gains its benefit until you finish another Long Rest. Each can use it once during that period. This increases to twice at Sorcerer level 6 and three times at level 11. Use the dreams button to record creatures, roll, and track uses.',
'When rolling for Fate of Dreams, you can roll twice and choose which dream applies. If both dice show the same number, you can choose any dream on the table. In addition, after a creature spends all its uses of Fate of Dreams, you can spend 1 Sorcery Point to roll again on the table and grant it one additional use of that new dream.',
'Whenever you take a Long Rest, you can communicate with another creature on the same plane as if using the Dream spell. You cannot take on a monstrous appearance as part of this effect.',
'Once on each of your turns, you can use up to 30 feet of your movement to teleport that distance. Your destination must be an unoccupied space you can see.',
'As an action, you cast Simulacrum targeting yourself. Instead of ice or snow, the simulacrum is made of the essence of your dreams. It lasts 1 hour, then dissipates. It can look however you wish, but cannot be more than one size larger than you. It has no spell slots above level 5 and can use Metamagic without spending Sorcery Points. It cannot use Manifest Vision. After using this action, you must finish a Long Rest to use it again, unless you spend 10 Sorcery Points to repeat it.'
];
