const LEGACY_EN559={
casting:'At Sorcerer level 1, you know four cantrips and two level 1 spells from the Sorcerer list. Charisma is your spellcasting ability. Your spell save DC is 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Charisma modifier; your spell attack modifier is Proficiency Bonus + Charisma modifier. You can use an arcane focus.\n\nThese spells are known, without daily preparation. Whenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one known spell with another from the list for which you have spell slots. Known-spell counts follow the 2014 table. Cantrips: four initially, five from level 4, and six from level 10. You regain expended spell slots when you finish a Long Rest.\n\nThe Codex’s shared spell catalog remains available; this option changes class progression without replacing every spell description with its 2014 version.',
origin:'Choose your subclass at Sorcerer level 1. It grants additional benefits at levels 6, 14, and 18. Dream Sorcery uses its original Planegea levels; Draconic Bloodline uses its 2014 progression.',
font:'Starting at level 2, your maximum Sorcery Points equal your Sorcerer level. You regain all expended points when you finish a Long Rest.\n\nAs a Bonus Action, you can spend points to create a spell slot: level 1 costs 2; level 2 costs 3; level 3 costs 5; level 4 costs 6; level 5 costs 7. These extra slots disappear after a Long Rest.\n\nAs a Bonus Action, you can also expend a spell slot to regain Sorcery Points equal to its level, without exceeding your maximum.',
meta:'At level 3, choose two Metamagic options. Choose another at level 10 and another at level 17, for four in total. You can apply only one option to a casting unless an option expressly allows a combination. Costs are paid with Sorcery Points.\n\n• Careful Spell (1 point): choose up to your Charisma modifier, minimum one, of the creatures forced to make a saving throw. They succeed on that saving throw.\n\n• Distant Spell (1 point): double a range of at least 5 feet; a range of Touch becomes 30 feet.\n\n• Empowered Spell (1 point): reroll up to your Charisma modifier damage dice, minimum one, and use the new results. Can be combined with another Metamagic option.\n\n• Extended Spell (1 point): double a spell’s duration if it lasts at least 1 minute, up to 24 hours.\n\n• Heightened Spell (3 points): one target has Disadvantage on its first saving throw against the spell.\n\n• Quickened Spell (2 points): a spell with a casting time of an action instead uses a Bonus Action for this casting.\n\n• Subtle Spell (1 point): the casting requires no Verbal or Somatic components. Material components are still required.\n\n• Twinned Spell (points equal to spell level, or 1 for a cantrip): add a second target within range to a spell that, at the level cast, cannot affect more than one creature and does not have a range of Self.',
asi:'Increase one ability score by 2 or two different scores by 1, without exceeding 20. If your table uses feats, you can choose a feat instead. At level 19, the 2014 Sorcerer receives this increase, not an automatic Epic Boon.',
restoration:'At level 20, you regain 4 expended Sorcery Points when you finish a Short Rest, without exceeding your maximum.',
ancestor:'Choose your dragon ancestry: Black or Copper (Acid); Blue or Bronze (Lightning); Brass, Gold, or Red (Fire); Green (Poison); Silver or White (Cold). This damage type is used by later benefits.\n\nYou speak, read, and write Draconic. When making a Charisma check to interact with dragons, double your Proficiency Bonus if it applies to the check.',
resilience:'Your maximum HP increase by 1 for each Sorcerer level, starting at level 1. While you wear no armor, your base AC is 13 + Dexterity modifier.',
affinity:'At level 6, when you cast a spell that deals your ancestor’s damage type, add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of that spell. At the same time, you can spend 1 Sorcery Point to gain Resistance to that damage type for 1 hour.',
wings:'At level 14, as a Bonus Action on your turn, you can manifest dragon wings and gain a Fly Speed equal to your current speed. They last until dismissed with another Bonus Action. Armor must be adapted to accommodate the wings; unsuitable clothing may be destroyed when they appear.',
presence:'At level 18, as an action, you can spend 5 Sorcery Points to create an aura of awe or fear extending 60 feet. For 1 minute, or until you lose Concentration as if concentrating on a spell, each hostile creature that starts its turn in the aura must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or be Charmed (awe) or Frightened (fear) until the aura ends. A creature that succeeds is immune to your aura for 24 hours.'
};
